      "id": "yzq53kt",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Mahatma Gandhi (1869–1948)"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Mahatma Gandhi (1869–1948) is listed as a central figure among India's freedom fighters.",
        "Subhas Chandra Bose's active life spanned from 1897 to 1945.",
        "Bhagat Singh (1907–1931) and Rani Lakshmibai (1828–1858) represent key historical timelines in the independence movement.",
        "Prominent leaders of the late 19th and early 20th century include Bal Gangadhar Tilak (1856–1920), Lala Lajpat Rai (1865–1928), and Bipin Chandra Pal (1858–1932).",
        "Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel (1875–1950) and Jawaharlal Nehru (1889–1964) form key components of modern Indian history syllabus."
      ],
      "id": "ebn23bk"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "odgswtp",
      "content": "• Known as the 'Father of the Nation'."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "eduut1q",
      "content": "• Leader of the Indian National Movement."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "t2yk6br",
      "content": "• Introduced Satyagraha and non-violent resistance."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2lbdcjl",
      "content": "• Led Non-Cooperation (1920), Civil Disobedience (1930), Quit India (1942)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qthrd5w",
      "content": "• Led the Dandi March in 1930."
    },
    {
      "id": "u42kban",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Subhas Chandra Bose (1897–1945)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mqydg31",
      "content": "• Popularly known as Netaji."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "w2oj59i",
      "content": "• Founded the Indian National Army (INA)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "uytwhzs",
      "content": "• Gave the slogan 'Give me blood and I will give you freedom'."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9uwvoof",
      "content": "• Formed the Azad Hind Government."
    },
    {
      "id": "nja6jms",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Bhagat Singh (1907–1931)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cddtkmq",
      "content": "• Famous revolutionary freedom fighter."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lusay9s",
      "content": "• Involved in the Lahore Conspiracy Case."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "uj8alct",
      "content": "• Along with Batukeshwar Dutt threw bombs in the Central Legislative Assembly in 1929."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "07vws3t",
      "content": "• Executed by the British in 1931."
    },
    {
      "id": "9889y6h",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Rani Lakshmibai (1828–1858)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5t8iq9j",
      "content": "• Queen of Jhansi and leader in the Revolt of 1857."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "eadp3f6",
      "content": "• Fought bravely against British forces."
    },
    {
      "id": "xr7x2hf",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Bal Gangadhar Tilak (1856–1920)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "efly496",
      "content": "• Known as the 'Father of Indian Unrest'."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "z6zv37w",
      "content": "• Gave slogan 'Swaraj is my birthright and I shall have it'."
    },
    {
      "id": "pvwt12y",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Lala Lajpat Rai (1865–1928)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jbrush6",
      "content": "• Known as 'Punjab Kesari'."
    },
